.TXT 6 9 17033 0 0
Cg a77.625000,77.625000,461
{\rtf\ansi \deff0{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue128;}{\fonttbl{\f0
\fcharset0\fnil Arial;}}\plain\cf1\fs20 \pard It is clear that the 
Fast Convolution Differential Method offers better performance over
\par the Discrete-time Difference Method, especially when the SNR is 
high.  The price \par paid for better performance is a higher number 
of calculations, but the price may \par be immaterial given today's 
technology.  It is also clear that the Hard-limiter and \par the 
Guassian window drastically improve performance under noise, as 
compared \par with both systems in the document FM2.MCD.  }
